WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.010
<i>My name is Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.540
<i>I'm a second year middle 
schooler who loves soccer.</i>

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>Although, I'm only the 
manager in the soccer club.</i>

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:14.260
<i>But unlike me, my brother, 
Suguru Aizawa, is truly amazing.</i>

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:18.390
<i>He's the genius soccer player 
known as "Japan's Treasure."</i>

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.460
<i>One day, while I was working as manager 
for my brother's team as usual,</i>

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.670
<i>my childhood friend Nana Mishima,</i>

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.960
<i>nicknamed Seven,</i>

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.700
<i>suddenly came back from America 
and transferred to our school.</i>

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.620
<i>Seven joined the club as a manager</i>

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.010
<i>and said, "let's do our best as managers,"</i>

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.880
<i>but my brother put me in the</i>

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.440
<i>selection match and told me 
to compete as a player.</i>

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.990
<b>The Knight in the Area</b>

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.600
Kunimatsu-san sure is relentless.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.460
He's completely blocking the pass 
path to the leading forward, Kakeru.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.170
But the white team's sideback 
has pulled too far back.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.030
Huh?

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.060
The defensive midfielder, 
Yuusuke-kun, is fine,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.830
but, as it is, the middle is
leaving too much open space,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.690
so if one penetrating pass gets 
through, they'll be in trouble.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.850
They need to feel the zone 
better and keep it compact.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.930
The red team's conductor 
is Suguru-san, after all.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.130
Um... so the defensive 
midfielder is in outer space

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.650
and Suguru-san is a compacter?

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.610
Nana-chan, you sure know your soccer.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.430
I am the manager, after all.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:05.590
Here it comes!

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.630
Yuusuke, mark him!

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:08.080
On it.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.380
<i>Right?</i>

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:14.790
<i>Or left?</i>

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.600
<i>Wait. This is...</i>

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:17.920
<i>a feint!</i>

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.340
<i>It's right!</i>

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.320
<i>Oh, shoot!</i>

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.860
A pass! To the opposite side?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.600
No. This pass is...

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.270
Straight for the goal.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.900
A pass to Kakeru.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.520
When did he get...

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.020
Man! So close!

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.560
Just a little further.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.650
A little?

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.770
He was two meters short.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:51.080
Even if the manager, Kakeru-kun, 
was able to reach the ball,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.880
he wouldn't have been able to score.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.660
Why you, Nishijima!

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.060
Don't come over here!

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.800
What? Where I watch from 
is my choice, isn't it?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.020
You started off too slow.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:00.960
Shut up!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.530
You should be able to get a ball like that.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.900
I'll get the next one.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.000
<b>Team/Period | First Half | Second Half | Overtime | PK | Total</b>

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.000
<b>White
Red</b>

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.730
That pass was just mean, 
no matter how you look at it.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.510
There was no getting it.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.700
And why aren't the other 
offensive players following?

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.770
They're leaving Kakeru to run by himself.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.830
It's not that they're not following; 
they <i>can't</i> follow.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.590
What?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.300
No one can keep up with the 
unexpectedness of Suguru-san's passes.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:43.970
No one, except Kakeru.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.830
Are you okay, Kakeru?

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.650
That Suguru's sending 
some impossible passes.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.120
Do you want to be subbed out?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.280
Just a little more...

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.280
Just a little more and I'll get it.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.440
Kakeru?

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.970
The white team's defense is getting better.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.850
Space was being left in the middle, 
but now the gaps are closed.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.840
It won't be easy,

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.650
even for Suguru-san,
 to make that pass to Kakeru.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.000
What? You're saying he'll keep 
sending that pass to Kakeru?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.050
Obviously.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.340
The rest of the offense can't keep up

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.630
with the speed of Suguru-san's passes.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.640
Only Kakeru is seriously 
calling for the ball.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.890
His eyes keep calling for that pass.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.370
Kakeru!

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.600
If you're a forward, you need to 
look like you want that pass.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.350
Call for it with your eyes.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.690
I'll definitely give you the 
pass, if you call for it.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.030
I'll stop him this time!

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.190
<i>I-I can't move...</i>

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.140
<i>If I close in, he'll pass it.</i>

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.400
<i>But if I fall back, he'll push 
forward with his dribble.</i>

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.090
<i>His killer intent is palpable.</i>

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:03.450
<i>This is what it feels like 
to face the U-15s' ace...</i>

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.510
Damn it!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:09.180
The ball!

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.800
<i>Getting a decisive pass into the area</i>

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.600
<i>doesn't happen by the 
power of the conductor alone.</i>

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.560
<i>When the forward moves towards 
a ball he can't even see yet,</i>

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.570
<i>The conductor's creativity 
creates a miracle.</i>

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.580
<i>A killer pass that cuts 
the field like magic.</i>

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.260
No way!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.290
There's no way he'll get it.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:40.800
<i>I'll get it!</i>

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.920
<i>There's no way my brother...</i>

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.300
<i>no way Suguru Aizawa would send 
a pass that I couldn't get!</i>

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.070
<i>I'll definitely get it!</i>

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.090
All right!

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.140
Shoot, Kakeru!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.670
Gooo!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:07.650
That was close.

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.320
Nice save, Tominaga!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:18.110
So close! That was a good 
save by the keeper.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:19.800
Normally, that would have scored.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.960
What are you talking about?

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.860
That was a totally easy save.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.210
Hey, Nishijima...

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:24.710
What?

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.200
Come out back with me!

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.270
I also think it was obvious that 
that shot was going to be stopped.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.100
What?

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.930
He should've shot that with his left.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.750
Instead, he took an extra step 
so he could shoot with his right.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.200
That gave the keeper an instant

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.170
to read the course of the shot.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.740
If he had shot with his left, 
 he would've scored.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.450
Get it, pointy-head?

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.770
Kakeru's always like this...

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:52.610
Always?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.580
Yeah. We all had huge expectations of him

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.040
when he joined the club 
at the start of middle school,

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.390
since he was Suguru-san's brother.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.310
But, even though he had 
technique and speed,

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.380
he was always kind of awkward.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.640
In matches he'd create opportunities,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.960
but his shots never went in.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.800
In the end, he never scored 
a point during scrimmages

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.390
or against other schools.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:20.350
So, he got the nickname "Mr. No Goal."

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:22.310
Kakeru...

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:27.270
<i>When I make a fast break, 
my brother will pass it to me.</i>

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.060
<i>I run and run and run,</i>

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:35.560
<i>and I finally receive 
that unsuppressed pass.</i>

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.240
<i>I'll put it in next time.</i>

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.240
<i>I'll definitely put it in!</i>

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.680
He went with his left!

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.500
Nice batting!

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.310
Aizawa hits a home run out of the field!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.590
All right. Next time.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.860
Sub out, Kakeru.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.820
What? B-But I still...

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:15.920
No buts about it.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.610
Go back to the bench and 
do your work as a manager.

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:19.700
That's...

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.200
We're subbing. Shigeo Nishijima, 
you're in for Kakeru Aizawa!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:24.910
Okay!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.110
See ya.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.300
That guy...

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.680
Kota Nakatsuka, go in as the left sideback.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.770
Yes! All right! I'm in!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:34.760
Do your best!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.120
Don't worry about it, Kakeru.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.550
You've still got your manager work.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:40.930
Right?

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.400
Kakeru.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.360
Good work, Kakeru.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.690
You did well out there.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.170
Here...

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.580
I'm not being sarcastic.
 I really think so.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.410
I'm not the only one, either.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:13.690
I'm sure that Suguru-san wanted 
to say, "good work," too.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:23.220
<b>Team/Period | First Half | Second Half | Overtime | PK | Total</b>

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:23.220
<b>White
Red</b>

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.280
Suguru-senpai sure is amazing.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.920
Between the assist for the first point

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.990
and the long shot for the second...

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.980
The recruit team won against the regular team

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.190
just because he played for them.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.220
On the other hand, 
I sure feel bad for Kakeru-san.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:36.410
It can't be helped.
 He's just the manager.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:41.580
My goal was half thanks to you, Suguru-san.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:43.630
That was a sweet pass.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.070
I don't know how anyone could 
miss with a pass like that.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.790
Oh, sorry.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:53.110
Even though you're brothers, 
I feel bad for Kakeru.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.550
His older brother took 
all the talent with him.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.420
I really sympathize.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.800
I'm counting on you until 
Ishikawa returns, Nishijima.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:05.510
You mean, when Ishikawa returns, 
I'm off the team?

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.310
Didn't I score today?

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:11.510
The only forward on our team who 
can easily get past Kunimatsu-san

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.890
and score is me!

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:13.510
Oh?

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:15.930
Easily get past me?

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.350
Ow!

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:18.950
It's true, isn't it?

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:20.470
I won today.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:24.240
Idiot. I was taken down by Kakeru, not you.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:25.640
Kakeru?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.180
It's an embarrassing story,

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.830
but his tricky moves had me doing

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.740
impossible sprints over and over again.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.220
My knees couldn't take it.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:37.440
But Kakeru missed pass after pass 
while I scored on the first one.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.580
You really didn't understand 
anything, did you?

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:41.840
During today's selection match,

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.490
the passes that Suguru was sending to Kakeru

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.330
were all serious passes.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:50.820
He's never even once passed like 
that to any of the regulars.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.860
A forward who can score on a pass 
like that could play nationally...

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.320
No, internationally.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.810
So what? You worked pretty hard today.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.490
I don't want someone who

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.290
was taken down by Kakeru 
to tell me I worked hard.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.680
What? That's not very cute!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.180
Where's the "thank you"?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.250
Ow!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.800
Suguru-san...

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.270
You want to say,
 "put Kakeru in a game," right?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.050
Yes.

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.230
You know it too, right?

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:41.760
Even if you're the conductor,

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.900
without a forward who can pick up your passes,

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.450
we can't compete in the nationals.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:49.070
It's no good.
 I can't use Kakeru in a match.

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.210
Why not?

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.860
The moment he went to get the pass,

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.510
he'd moved into the defender's blind spot

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.380
or slipped past them with a feint.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.130
He's got the perfect moves 
 for a top scorer.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.070
Even though he was being so

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.550
tightly marked by Kunimatsu-san,

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.640
he was always aware of the goal

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:06.300
and he picked up your passes many times.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.690
I was also surprised by his stamina.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:12.720
Kakeru's been the manager 
since second year, right?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.310
Yet, even after running around that much,

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.440
his speed didn't drop at all.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.500
That's why Kunimatsu-san, 
who had been marking Kakeru,

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.300
was exhausted by the time

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.280
Nishijima was subbed in, 
and he was able to score.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.250
He picked up your serious passes

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.090
and was even able to 
attempt a shot at the end.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.330
It's true that he wasn't able to score,

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.980
but he was able to create so many chances.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.300
That's why.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.820
In a close match,

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:40.790
the most important thing is to 
never let a chance pass you by.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.380
Miss that many shots and what happens?

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.670
The team's motivation falls...

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:47.400
Exactly.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.240
Even if Kakeru makes chances,

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.810
if he doesn't score,
 it amounts to zero.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.060
Maybe even less than zero.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:55.800
That's soccer.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.060
But...

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:02.520
What Kakeru lacks isn't skill or stamina.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:05.500
It's heart.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:08.730
It's the same reason why he avoids his left.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.150
Suguru-san.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.730
I thought if I put him in a match,

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.320
he would change a little, but...

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:21.970
Kakeru!

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.600
Suguru-san has high hopes for you, Kakeru.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.840
That's why—

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.720
My brother's right.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:32.100
Those with weak hearts aren't 
meant for soccer, right?

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.770
There's no need to humiliate me.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.750
I get it.

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.050
Kakeru...

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.570
So Nana-chan became a manager.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:51.450
So...

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.950
Has she gotten cuter?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.810
Huh? Um... no, not really...

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:56.650
You fell for her!

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:58.100
Why do you jump to that?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:59.160
You're wrong!

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.230
Kake-nii's been in love with Seven

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.710
ever since elementary school.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.450
Huh? Am I wrong?

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.460
That's what it seemed like.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:09.380
After she moved away, you were 
watching the sunset and crying.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.720
Cut it out!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.430
What? Kake-nii, you seem kind of down.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.840
I'm tired from practice.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:16.610
I'm home.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:17.990
Welcome home.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:18.900
Welcome home...

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.000
Thank you for the meal.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.830
Oh. Are you done already?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.720
Suguru, you come home late every night.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:26.730
I have practice.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.420
Oh, you're on the <i>ball</i>.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.400
That's terrible.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.700
That was my <i>goal</i>.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.110
Hey. I waited for you.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.960
I had a feeling that you 
might be here again tonight.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.440
I don't who you are,

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.890
but do you think you could 
go all out with me tonight?

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.460
Oh, this?

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.800
Don't worry about it.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.890
I just really wanted to wear this tonight.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.220
During my two years in middle school,

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:06.500
I never received a number, 
but I've always practiced in this.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:09.130
My middle school soccer experience

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:11.360
has been like this uniform with no number.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.490
All right. Let's get started.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:15.820
Here I come!

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.550
<i>I'm going to enjoy this with all my strength!</i>

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:21.320
<i>With all my strength...</i>

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:40.770
End of the first half.

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.530
Middle school soccer has a thirty minute half,

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:45.230
so let's take a break here.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.690
I must look like an idiot, right?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.320
I'm just the manager, 
but I do this every day.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.780
It's like I don't know when to give up.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.050
Here. You're thirsty, right?

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.860
I don't know who you are,

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:05.710
but you know that I have a weak left.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.800
When I was in elementary school, 
during a practice match,

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.320
I caused one of the other regulars to

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.760
suffer a serious injury 
because of my left kick.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.090
He tore a ligament in his knee

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.090
and his leg bent in a weird direction.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:22.760
The ambulance came and
 took him away on a stretcher.

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:26.480
Since then, I've been afraid 
of kicking with my left.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.510
Well... it's just an excuse.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.480
All right! It's a little early,
 but half time over.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.400
Let's start the second half.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:48.710
Wait up!

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:49.340
Hey!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.900
Why?

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.630
You're home late.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:02.890
At the convenience store again?

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:06.530
Hey, Kakeru. 
What were you doing?

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:10.480
Stop playing dumb.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.730
Why won't you come out and say it?!

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:14.510
You have something to say, right?

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.240
Then just be clear about it!

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:19.860
Hey, Kake-nii. Cut it out.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.490
You two have been acting 
weird since yesterday.

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:27.150
What's wrong with you?

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.930
Sugu-nii, it's breakfast time.

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.840
Good morning.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.850
You're awfully chipper this morning.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.200
I was worried since you 
were fighting yesterday.

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:42.660
Here.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.870
Mother, where's Kakeru?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.870
Surprisingly, he left 
early this morning. Why?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.110
It's nothing. 
Man, I'm hungry.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.950
A flat?

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.670
This isn't my day.

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:01.450
I won't make it to morning 
practice like this.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:04.010
I guess it doesn't really matter.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.430
After today, I'm...

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.350
What's wrong, Kakeru?

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:13.190
My bike got a flat.

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:55.650
This reminds me of when we were younger.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.660
I couldn't ride a bike yet,

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.930
so I ran desperately to keep up with you.

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.610
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.170
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.420
It's okay.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:18.020
I attacked you the day before,
 so we're even.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:25.180
Kakeru, I have something to 
talk to you about before practice.

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.640
Me too, brother.

00:21:28.940 --> 00:21:32.100
Actually, I was thinking of 
telling you after practice,

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.210
but I'll say it now.

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.980
I want to get it off my chest.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.820
I'm quitting the soccer club.

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:43.690
I was pretending

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.940
to want to pursue being a manager.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.610
But I was half-hearted.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.160
I want a clean break.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:53.240
No matter what?

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:55.810
No matter what.

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:57.560
I see...

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:01.590
But... I still want you 
to give it your best.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.840
You don't have to worry about me anymore.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.230
Become greater and greater,

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:08.400
and represent Japan as a conductor.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.820
I want you to stand in the

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:12.260
middle of the field and shine like a king.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:17.280
Because, in the end, I like your soccer.

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:21.230
The king of the field...

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:23.760
But you know, Kakeru,

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:26.750
even if a king fights 
with everything he's got,

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:28.610
he can't win by himself.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:29.780
Brother...

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:34.160
If the conductor is the 
king of the field,

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:35.550
then the striker is the knight.

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:36.990
I need—

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:43.270
No. Japan needs a knight 
who can receive passes

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:47.170
in the penalty area and open 
a path towards the goal.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:49.890
A knight in the area.

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:53.590
A knight in the area?

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:56.140
You're amazing, brother.

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:59.300
Even though you're only 
a year older than me.

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:01.220
You must be able to see yourself

00:23:01.220 --> 00:23:04.860
standing on the field of the World Cup.

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:07.310
A knight in the area...

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:08.560
I'm sure there is one.

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.070
A striker who can receive

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:15.070
your magical passes and 
send them on into the goal.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:16.790
What?

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:21.520
Kakeru, I had a dream this morning.

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.250
A dream?

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:24.640
Yeah, the best dream.

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.440
I was wearing the national blue uniform

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:29.130
and I was standing on the field.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.760
It was the finals of the World Cup.

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:33.430
The score was 0-0 in extra time.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:35.470
I sent a through pass 
towards the front line.

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:39.600
The ball flew through a hole in 
the defense and into the area.

00:23:40.820 --> 00:23:44.060
Kakeru, who do you think it was...

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:48.000
who received that pass?

00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:14.520
This is terrible.

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:16.380
They said someone fell asleep at the wheel.

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:17.850
Two middle school students...

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.410
How sad!

00:24:24.370 --> 00:24:26.480
A bag from our school?

00:24:26.990 --> 00:24:27.980
It couldn't be!

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:34.430
Excuse me. Excuse me.

00:24:37.480 --> 00:24:39.680
S-Suguru-san!

00:24:40.190 --> 00:24:42.250
Kakeru!

00:24:45.920 --> 00:25:15.450
<b>Next time:
A Brother's Pulse</b>

00:24:47.820 --> 00:24:48.880
Suguru and Kakeru.

00:24:49.600 --> 00:24:50.960
The precious dreams

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:54.760
of soccer that the two 
brothers had always had

00:24:54.760 --> 00:24:56.800
are about to be lost.

00:24:57.540 --> 00:25:00.430
To those two, who had walked 
the same path for so long,

00:25:00.430 --> 00:25:04.310
an unthinkable time of 
parting was approaching.

00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:07.180
Next time on The Knight in the Area:

00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:09.860
the third episode,
 "A Brother's Pulse."

00:25:10.460 --> 00:25:13.490
Don't go! Suguru-san! Kakeru!
